(a) Operator. Only persons 16 years of age or older and holding a valid driver's license may operate a personal transportation vehicle (PTV) on the designated streets within the city, per section 54-44.
(b) Occupants. The number of occupants in a personal transportation vehicle (PTV) shall be limited to the number of persons for whom factory seating is installed and provided on the PTV. The operator or any occupant shall be seated in the PTV and no parts of the bodies of the operator or any occupant shall extend outside the perimeter of the PTV while the PTV is being operated.
(c) Operation hours. A personal transportation vehicle (PTV) may be operated only during daylight hours between one-half hour before sunrise and one-half hour after sunset, unless equipped with two operating headlights, tail lights, and brake lights that are visible from a distance of 500 feet. PTVs shall not be operated at any time when there is insufficient light to clearly see persons or vehicles on the street at a distance of 500 feet.
(d) Traffic rules. The operator of the personal transportation vehicle (PTV) shall comply with all traffic rules and regulations adopted by the State of Georgia O.C.G.A. Title 40, Article 6 as well Chapter 54 of the City Code which govern the operation of motor vehicles. No operator or occupant shall engage in hazardous activities. Such hazardous activities include, but are not limited to, the following:
(1) Racing of any kind;
(2) Blocking of public access;
(3) Loitering or parking on streets, bridges or in underpasses;
(4) Pedestrians should be given due consideration and reasonable right-of-way to ensure safe passage;
(5) An audible warning shall be given by operators of PTVs when approaching pedestrians from the rear;
(6) All laws and ordinances relative to alcohol and the use thereof, including open container laws, apply to the operator and occupants of PTVs.
(e) Insurance. The operator or owner of a personal transportation vehicle (PTV) shall have written proof of insurance. Documentation of such coverage must be kept on the PTV or carried by the person operating the PTV.
(Ord. No. 2022-10-26, § 1, 10-17-2022)
